Notes:      Dimension values (M2–M12 where the standard defines them)
            transcribed into two independent, purpose-specific
            representations — Rust metadata tables
            (onecad-library::tables) and C++ worker generator tables
            (FastenerTables.cpp) — per this project's architecture
            (generators are built-in/versioned in the worker; the library
            crate serves authoring/metadata, not geometry). Neither copy
            embeds BOLTS source code, only the published dimension data.
            The repository's GitHub-reported top-level license (GPL-3.0)
            is a whole-repo default; the specific data files used here
            carry their own LGPL 2.1+ headers, which is the license that
            applies to this data.

            ONE CORRECTION was made to the BOLTS values: ISO 7089's M10
            inner diameter is listed there as 10.0 mm. ISO 7089 and DIN
            125 A (which that BOLTS table is anchored to) both publish
            10.5 mm, and a 10.0 mm bore would not pass an M10 bolt. Both
            copies use 10.5 and pin it with a test. Every other value is
            verbatim from the source.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------
Not third-party — hand-transcribed public standards
-------------------------------------------------------------------------

The following dimension data is NOT from BOLTS or any other third-party
dataset, and is listed here only so its provenance is not mistaken for the
above. It was hand-transcribed from the published dimension tables of the
named standards, which are numeric facts rather than a licensed work:

  * ISO 7380-1 button head socket screw (dk, k) — not present in BOLTS
    (data/hex_socket.blt carries no button-head class).
  * ISO 7093-1 plain washer, large series (d1, d2, s) — not present in
    BOLTS (data/washer.blt carries 7089/7090/7091/7092 only).
  * ISO 261 coarse thread pitch series (pitch_mm), used by every threaded
    family.
